<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mustapha Harun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918–1995</span> · Also known as Tun Mustapha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mustapha Harun was a Malaysian politician from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabah">Sabah</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suluk">Suluk</a> and Bajau descent. A leading figure in the negotiations that brought North <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a> into Malaysia in 1963, he became Sabah's first head of state and, as chief minister from 1967 to 1975, dominated the state's politics through his party, the United Sabah National Organisation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mustapha-harun.jpg" alt="Mustapha Harun" width="175" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mustapha_Harun.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
